{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"creased-mutinous-mammoth","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Observation\n\nThe Lambda `bedrock-principal-audit` (us-east-1, description \"Daily drift audit: Bedrock-capable IAM principals vs spend-cap enrollment\", publishes to SNS topic `bedrock-spend-cap-alerts`) runs once a day at about 14:00 UTC (07:00 PDT) and emits a JSON report. Its `/aws/lambda/bedrock-principal-audit` log group over the last 60 days shows:\n\n- 2026-09-13 04:17 UTC: first run, `drift: [\"role/OrganizationAccountAccessRole\"]`. 32 seconds later a second run reports `drift: []` with that role in `enrolled_roles`, so the role was enrolled at deploy time.\n- 2026-09-13 through 2026-09-20: `drift: []` every day.\n- 2026-09-21 14:00 UTC onward: `drift: [\"role/OrganizationAccountAccessRole\"]` on every daily run, 28 consecutive days through 2026-10-18, with no change in the report.\n- 2026-09-24: one run also listed an IAM user with a `bakeoff-rebar-re…` prefix as drift; it did not recur.\n\nThe spend-cap Lambda `bedrock-spend-cap` (last modified 2026-09-25 16:03 UTC) carries the enrollment list in its `TARGET_ROLES` environment variable: 11 roles (`lmn-*`, `rebar-external-ci-bedrock`, `rebar-gerrit-instance-role`) plus `TARGET_GROUPS=Admin`. `OrganizationAccountAccessRole` is not in that list. The role has `AdministratorAccess` attached, so it is Bedrock-capable, which is exactly the condition the audit flags.\n\nSo the alarm is correct about the state and recurs because the state never changes: the role was de-enrolled (or the enrollment list was rebuilt without it) between the 2026-09-20 and 2026-09-21 runs, and no one has either re-enrolled it or taught the audit that it is an accepted exception.\n\n## What is not yet established\n\n- Whether dropping the role from `TARGET_ROLES` was deliberate. The spend-cap deny policy attaches to enrolled principals when the cap trips; enrolling the organisation access role would mean a tripped cap also denies Bedrock to the org-level admin path, which may be the reason it was removed. That decision is not recorded anywhere I could find (no ticket matches `principal audit`, `drift`, or `OrganizationAccountAccessRole`).\n- Where the audit Lambda's source lives. `git grep enrolled_roles` across all local branches finds nothing, and `infra/` has no `principal-audit` reference, so the deployed code is not in this repository.\n- Whether the SNS message is what the operator sees as \"the recurring enrollment alarm\", or whether a CloudWatch alarm sits on top (no CloudWatch alarm or metric filter references the audit log group).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- AC1: The 2026-09-21 de-enrollment is explained from evidence (CloudTrail `UpdateFunctionConfiguration` on `bedrock-spend-cap`, or the deploy that rebuilt `TARGET_ROLES`) and the finding is recorded on this ticket.\n- AC2: A decision is recorded, as a comment here and in the runbook, on whether `OrganizationAccountAccessRole` is enrolled in the cap or is an accepted exception, with the reasoning (what a tripped cap would deny if it is enrolled).\n- AC3: The audit implements that decision: either the role is re-added to `TARGET_ROLES`, or the audit gains an explicit allow-list of accepted exceptions so an acknowledged principal stops firing daily. An unacknowledged new principal must still fire.\n- AC4: The audit Lambda's source is checked in under `infra/` (or its location is documented in the spend-cap runbook) so the next operator can change it without reverse-engineering the deployed artifact.\n- AC5: The day after the change lands, the daily audit run reports `drift: []`, confirmed from the log group and noted here.\n\n## Notes\n\n- No spend figures or thresholds belong on this ticket; the tickets branch is public. The cap's numeric configuration is readable from the Lambda environment by an operator with the `frontier` profile.\n- Related: the spend-cap work landed through recent commits on main (`bedrock-spend-cap: fix marketplace rate units`, `Price the Bedrock cap at a per-direction ceiling`, `Monitor the Bedrock cap's upper-bound invariant`).","id":"48c5-c32c-637e-4516","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["aws","bedrock","spend-cap","ops","alarm"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"bedrock-principal-audit reports OrganizationAccountAccessRole as enrollment drift every day since 2026-09-21; the alarm recurs because nothing resolves or acknowledges it"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1792360488994135387,"uuid":"3f1f3b66-586f-4815-93ae-fd5770cb203e"}